# Changelog on Push

Before running `git push`, update the changelog in `src/app/feedback/page.tsx`.

## When to update

Update the changelog whenever a push includes user-facing changes (features, fixes, UI, docs shown in-app). Skip only for purely internal or tooling-only commits with no user-visible effect.

## How to update

Add a **new object at the top** of the `changelogs` array (before the existing first entry):

```typescript
{
  version: "v1.3.6",           // increment patch from the current latest entry
  subtitle: "Short Title",   // optional but preferred for feature releases
  date: "Late-May 2026",       // match existing date style
  changes: [
    "User-facing change written in plain language",
    "Another bullet if needed",
  ],
},
```

## Workflow

1. Finish code changes and commit them.
2. Add the changelog entry summarizing what shipped.
3. Commit the changelog update (same commit or a follow-up `chore: update changelog` commit).
4. Push to GitHub.

Never push code changes without a matching changelog entry in the same push.
